Plug-ins: RSS, Sieve, calendar
- They are built into the program and loaded the first time Claws Mail
  starts. Configuration > Plugins lists them; Unload one you don't want
  (it stays unloaded), or Load... it again from the plugins folder.
  Their settings are in Choices... > Plugins.
- RSS (RSSyl): Menu on "My Feeds" in the folder list > Subscribe to
  feed..., and give the feed's address (http or https). Each feed is a
  folder; its items arrive as messages, and are fetched again on Get
  Mail or Menu > Refresh feed. Feeds are fetched one at a time: the
  desktop waits while one comes in.
- Sieve (ManageSieve): filters kept on your mail server, which sort or
  answer your mail there. Set it up for an account in Configuration >
  Edit accounts > the account > Plugins > Sieve (server, STARTTLS, log
  in), then Tools > Manage Sieve Filters... lists, edits and switches
  them on.
- Calendar (vCalendar): the "vCalendar" folder holds your meetings, in
  day, week and month views. A mail with a meeting invitation shows it,
  with Accept, Tentatively accept and Decline. Message > Create meeting
  from message, and Menu on vCalendar > New meeting... make one. Menu on
  vCalendar > Subscribe to Webcal... adds a published calendar
  (webcal:// or https://), fetched again on Get Mail. Time zones come
  from the application (share.zoneinfo).
